      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10759803::rubric_card::000::1894dec07a"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding approximately 4 at.% Cr to HfMoTaTiZr produces a Laves phase in addition to the BCC phase.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10759803::rubric_card::000::1894dec07a"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Cr-induced Laves phase has a low volume fraction of approximately 3–4%.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Cr-induced Laves phase consists of fine, coherently dispersed precipitates within a continuous BCC matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Laves phase impedes dislocation motion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Laves phase transfers load from the BCC matrix.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Laves phase deflects propagating cracks.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Cr-modified alloy has a yield strength approximately 200 MPa, or 13–15%, higher than the baseline alloy at room temperature.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10759803::rubric_card::000::1894dec07a"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Cr-modified alloy has approximately 20% greater fracture strain than the baseline alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The strength and ductility improvements persist at elevated temperatures up to approximately 800 °C.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Cr-induced Laves phase has a high melting point and strong interfacial bonding with the BCC matrix.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Cr-induced Laves phase remains stable without detrimental coarsening at temperatures up to approximately 800 °C.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Laves-phase interfaces act as effective irradiation-defect sinks.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Cr-modified alloy retains irradiation stability at moderate damage doses around 8 dpa.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
